course: dictionary
lesson: 8058
title: Reinforcement: stronger or rewarded
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reinforcement is a noun with more than one meaning. The words around it in the sentence tell you which meaning fits, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: In building and history, reinforcement means extra strength or extra people. Steel bars inside concrete are steel reinforcement. In a battle story, «Send reinforcements!» means send extra soldiers or helpers to give support when a side is losing.
explain: In training and school, reinforcement means a reward that makes a behaviour more likely to happen again. «A reward given straight after an action makes that action more likely; this is called positive reinforcement.» To check your meaning, swap in "reward or praise" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Reinforcement means something that makes another thing stronger, or extra help sent to support someone.
fact: «Reinforcements» (plural) are extra soldiers, police or helpers sent to give support.
fact: «Positive reinforcement» means a reward or praise that makes a behaviour more likely to happen again.
fact: Steel reinforcement, such as steel bars inside concrete, makes the building material stronger.
fact: Positive reinforcement is used for dogs, horses and dolphins, and even fish have learned to come to a target for a reward.
exercise: «Send reinforcements!» is shouted when a side is losing. What are reinforcements? | *Extra soldiers or helpers sent to give support | Quiet lessons with no homework | Wooden bars used to make a fence | Broken bridges that need to be cleared
exercise: A teacher praises a pupil the moment she answers well, so she is more likely to answer well again. What is this called? | *Positive reinforcement | Reinforcements | Steel reinforcement | Concrete mixing
exercise: Which is an example of steel reinforcement? | *Steel bars set inside concrete to make it stronger | A rusty gate left out in the rain | A steel spoon left in a drawer | Concrete poured with nothing inside it
test: «A reward given straight after an action makes that action more likely; this is called positive reinforcement.» What does positive reinforcement mean? | A reward given long after the action | *A reward or praise that makes a behaviour more likely | A punishment that stops a behaviour | A sudden loud noise
test: «Reinforcements arrived: 40 more soldiers.» What does reinforcements mean in this sentence? | Soldiers who have gone home | *Extra soldiers sent to help | Maps of the battle | Broken weapons
exam: A dog sits, and a clicker and a treat follow at once, so it learns to sit again. What is this training method called? | *Positive reinforcement | Steel reinforcement | Negative guessing | Reinforcements
